  "notes": "West leads the ♦J against 6♥. West's diamond lead should be ducked in dummy. The contract will be in danger only if clubs are 4-1. In that case, a second diamond trick will be the last hope for the contract.\n\nWhen East wins the ♦K, South appears to have 12 certain tricks (the ♠A, 6 hearts, 2 diamonds, and 3 clubs). The blockage in diamonds will be trouble if East returns a spade. South will be unable to enjoy both diamond tricks and the contract will be in jeopardy.\n\nSouth should unblock the ♦Q at trick 1. The spade shift is won in dummy and trumps are drawn. South should test clubs by cashing 2 rounds. If clubs are 4-1, South can finesse West for the ♦10 (his ♦J lead virtually guarantees the ♦10). Dummy's diamond will provide a discard for South's club loser.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♦J against 6♥. West's diamond lead should be ducked in dummy. The contract will be in danger only if clubs are 4-1. In that case, a second diamond trick will be the last hope for the contract.",
